Findings:

- **STATUS CODE REPORTING THE WRAPPER / check cannot fail**, line 113: exact input `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json = ["p.html"]`, `p.html = '<section class="panel" id="pn-protocol"><div class="absent-state"></div></section><script>document.querySelector(".absent-state").remove()</script>'`; consequence: the script can print `*** DIFFERS ***` and still exit `0`, so CI treats a proved mismatch as pass.

- **Probe keyed to the string a fix removes**, lines 76 and 113: exact input `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json = ["p.html"]`, `p.html = '<section id="pn-protocol" class="panel"><div class="absent-state"></div></section>'`; consequence: equivalent reordered attributes make `g3` empty, sample `0`, and the verifier exits `0` without measuring the page.

- **Idempotency guard satisfied by its own marker/comment**, lines 37 and 76: exact input `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json = ["p.html"]`, `p.html = '<!-- <section class="panel" id="pn-protocol"> -->'`; consequence: a comment is selected and classified as a real held panel, so marker text can satisfy the census.

- **Off-by-one / incomplete count**, line 80: exact input `PAGE_MAP.json = ["p00.html","p01.html","p02.html","p03.html","p04.html","p05.html","p06.html","p07.html","p08.html","p09.html","p10.html"]`, with `p00`-`p09` each exactly `<section class="panel" id="pn-protocol"></section>` and `p10` the differing script input from finding 1; consequence: `p10.html` is never sampled, so a known bad mapped page cannot fail the run.

- **Absent conflated with blank**, lines 96-101: exact input `ssot/PAGE_MAP.json = ["p.html"]`, `p.html = '<section class="panel" id="pn-protocol"></section>'`; consequence: the seven missing expected tabs become `" "` on both sides and count as `AGREE`.

No finding in this pasted module for CRLF text comparison, merged cells, or negation-dropped extraction. COULD NOT DETERMINE different-copy defect: missing caller/CI/deployment target defining whether worktree, HEAD, origin, or served pages are intended.
